Unemployment at 6.1% with payrolls averaging 272k and the fed funds rate at 0.09% points to mid-2014. The unemployment rate was 6.1% in both May and June 2014, and 6.3% in April. Payrolls averaged about 272k over the 3 months to June 2014 (April 304k, May 224k, June 267k, giving roughly 265k with revisions).

CPI YoY of 2.08% fits May 2014 (2.1%) or June 2014 (2.1%). Core CPI at 1.93% fits June 2014 (1.9%). The 10-year yield at 2.57% fits end of June 2014 (about 2.53%) or July 2014 (2.58%). US large-cap equity returned -2.0% over 1 month, which does not match June 2014, when the S&P rose. July 2014 saw the S&P fall about 1.4%, and developed ex-US fell about 3.5% that month. Gold fell 3.4% in July 2014? Gold dropped about 3% in July 2014, and the dollar rose that month. So July 2014 is plausible. The unemployment rate in July 2014 was 6.2% as first published, but later revisions put it at 6.1%. Payrolls in July were 212k, so the 3-month average of 267k, 288k and 212k is about 255k. The 10-year yield at 2.57% matches July. I'll go with July 2014.

